======================================================================
MODULE 14 : AGILE METHODOLOGY
TOPIC 2 : SCRUM FRAMEWORK – ROLES, CEREMONIES & ARTIFACTS
======================================================================

Q1. Who is a Scrum Master, and what are their responsibilities?

Interview Ready Answer

A Scrum Master is a servant leader and facilitator of the Scrum Team.
They ensure Scrum principles and practices are followed, facilitate
Scrum ceremonies, remove impediments (blockers), coach the team on
Agile practices, and help improve team productivity.

Definition

A Scrum Master is responsible for ensuring the Scrum framework is
properly followed.

Purpose

• Facilitate Scrum ceremonies.
• Remove impediments.
• Coach the team on Scrum.
• Ensure Scrum practices are followed.

======================================================================

Q2. Who is the Product Owner, and what are their responsibilities?

Interview Ready Answer

The Product Owner represents the customer and is responsible for
maximizing the value of the product. They create and prioritize the
Product Backlog, gather business requirements, communicate with
stakeholders, and ensure the team develops the highest-value features.

Definition

The Product Owner manages the Product Backlog and decides what should
be built first.

Purpose

• Gather customer requirements.
• Prioritize Product Backlog.
• Maximize business value.
• Communicate with stakeholders.

======================================================================

Q3. Who are the Development Team, and what are their responsibilities?

Interview Ready Answer

The Development Team is a cross-functional, self-managing team
responsible for designing, developing, testing, and delivering a
potentially shippable product increment in every Sprint.

Definition

The Development Team builds the product.

Purpose

• Develop product features.
• Test the application.
• Estimate Story Points.
• Deliver a working Increment.

======================================================================

Q4. What is Sprint Planning, and what is its purpose?

Interview Ready Answer

Sprint Planning is the first Scrum ceremony conducted at the beginning
of every Sprint. During this meeting, the Product Owner, Scrum Master,
and Development Team decide which Product Backlog items can be
completed in the upcoming Sprint. The selected items become the Sprint
Backlog, and the team defines the Sprint Goal.

Purpose

• Select Product Backlog items.
• Create Sprint Backlog.
• Define Sprint Goal.
• Plan work for the Sprint.

======================================================================

Q5. What is the purpose of the Daily Scrum?

Interview Ready Answer

The Daily Scrum is a 15-minute daily meeting where the Development Team
synchronizes work, tracks Sprint progress, and identifies impediments.

Each member typically answers:

• What did I complete yesterday?
• What will I work on today?
• Are there any blockers?

Purpose

• Track Sprint progress.
• Synchronize team work.
• Identify blockers.
• Keep everyone aligned.

======================================================================

Q6. What is Sprint Review, and what is its purpose?

Interview Ready Answer

Sprint Review is conducted at the end of the Sprint to demonstrate the
completed Increment to stakeholders. Feedback is collected and the
Product Backlog may be updated based on new requirements.

Purpose

• Demonstrate completed work.
• Collect stakeholder feedback.
• Update Product Backlog.
• Validate business expectations.

======================================================================

Q7. What is Sprint Retrospective, and what is its purpose?

Interview Ready Answer

Sprint Retrospective is the final Scrum ceremony where the Scrum Team
reflects on the completed Sprint to identify what went well, what did
not go well, and how the next Sprint can be improved.

Purpose

• Improve team process.
• Improve collaboration.
• Identify improvements.
• Continuous improvement.

======================================================================

Q8. What is a Product Backlog?

Interview Ready Answer

The Product Backlog is a prioritized list of all features,
enhancements, bug fixes, and tasks required to build the product. It is
managed and prioritized by the Product Owner.

Purpose

• Store all product requirements.
• Prioritize work.
• Guide future Sprints.

======================================================================

Q9. What is a Sprint Backlog?

Interview Ready Answer

The Sprint Backlog is the set of Product Backlog items selected for the
current Sprint, along with the plan to complete them.

Purpose

• Define Sprint work.
• Track Sprint tasks.
• Help achieve the Sprint Goal.

Difference

Product Backlog
• Entire product work.
• Managed by Product Owner.

Sprint Backlog
• Current Sprint work only.
• Selected during Sprint Planning.

======================================================================

Q10. What is an Increment?

Interview Ready Answer

An Increment is the working product produced at the end of a Sprint. It
contains all completed Product Backlog items that satisfy the
Definition of Done and is potentially releasable.

Purpose

• Deliver working software.
• Add business value after every Sprint.

======================================================================

Q11. What is the Definition of Done (DoD)?

Interview Ready Answer

Definition of Done (DoD) is a predefined checklist that determines
whether a Product Backlog item or Increment is considered complete. It
ensures the work has been developed, tested, reviewed, integrated,
meets quality standards, and is potentially releasable.

Purpose

• Maintain quality.
• Ensure consistent completion criteria.
• Prevent incomplete work from being accepted.

======================================================================
INTERVIEW TRAP QUESTIONS
======================================================================

Q1. Who prioritizes the Product Backlog?

Answer:
Product Owner.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Who estimates Story Points?

Answer:
Development Team.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Does the Scrum Master assign tasks to developers?

Answer:
No. The Development Team is self-managing.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q4. Is Sprint Review the same as Sprint Retrospective?

Answer:
No.

Sprint Review → Review the Product with stakeholders.

Sprint Retrospective → Review the team's process and identify
improvements.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Is Product Owner responsible for Story Point estimation?

Answer:
No. Story Points are estimated by the Development Team.

------------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Does Definition of Done mean Product Owner approval?

Answer:
No. DoD is a predefined quality checklist. Product Owner acceptance is
separate.

